From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:53:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(energy): Food, the coach, the week and the workout
 detail on the day model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FoodEnergy (the "largest candidate wins" resolver) and TrainingEnergy.extraKcal/extraByDay are gone;
EnergySource with them. The food card shows the model's burn with one short tag of what it lacks (no
steps · steps estimated · a workout without data), the workouts' share, and no burn at all without a
profile; the balance comes from the same figure. The coach's TODAY carries the burn with its parts
(basal, steps, workouts, after-burn, unlogged activity, digestion) and what is missing; ENERGY BALANCE
reads whole days only; MEASURED names its kcal per kg. The week's prompt gives each workout the model's
figure and how it was priced, and marks partly logged days. The workout detail shows the model's gross,
the method (heart rate / Claude / MET / import / steps) and what it adds to the day; Claude's own
estimate stays as a second line when it differs. The row keeps its kcal untouched (applyToRow takes the
Effort only). Claude's kcal prompt: the pulse OVER-reads lifting (pressor response), Compendium 2024
anchors (3.5 / 5.0 / 6.0 MET, HIIT 7-11), GROSS kcal; stored analyses are not re-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
